      mp3: 
      ms: 5160
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'male|a||It belongs between the two bars we have, and nobody can measure its height: those people did sign up.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:x6f3ic'
    male|a||In our town, say, coverage adds three good days to the people who took it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:16z8vkq'
    male|a||Your turn first. Coverage added three good days for them. How many would the insured have had without it? Set the middle bar.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:mw86ln'
    'male|a||Fifteen: without coverage, they would have been the least healthy group of all.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4960
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Now the quick comparison can be split at that middle bar.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:9yiuiw'
    male|a||Take the insured with coverage, minus the same people without it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:nmxu96'
    'male|a||Eighteen minus fifteen: three days, the effect of coverage on the people who took it. Economists call it the average treatment effect on the treated.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:3uuei9'
    male|a||Then add the insured without coverage, minus the uninsured without coverage.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:utcc0e'
    'male|a||Fifteen minus twenty-two: minus seven.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1kycjjp'
    male|a||Both halves of that second term are lives without coverage, so insurance is not in it at all.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:md9ssk'
    male|a||It measures only how the two groups of people differ. That is selection bias.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1qbbp5y'
    'male|a||Effect plus bias: three plus minus seven gives back the minus four we started with.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:19qvue9'
    male|a||So the quick comparison did its arithmetic right. It just answers a mixed question, and the bias here is more than twice the effect.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:81ki'
    male|a||And no data set tells us how big the second term is, because one half of it is the bar nobody sees.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1w6nv4j'
    male|a||So whether a raw gap flatters insurance or slanders it depends on the sign of that second term.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Across, the selection bias in good days; up, the gap the quick comparison shows.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:i1wzlt'
    male|a||The true effect stays at three, whatever the selection.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:vepn5u'
    male|a||The quick comparison is that three plus the bias, so it climbs one for one.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1mw1n3i'
    male|a||Our town sits at minus seven, which gives the minus four.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:da8nus'
    'male|a||Anywhere left of minus three, the comparison gets even the sign wrong: the bias outweighs the effect.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:4aablf'
    male|a||Watch the point slide toward zero and past it, and see where the quick comparison crosses the axis.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:14cnqa6'
    male|a||At minus three the bias cancels the effect, and the comparison reads zero.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Between minus three and zero the sign comes out right, but the effect is understated.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:j1ig8o'
    male|a||Right of zero, the bias adds to the effect, and the comparison overstates it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:13uzngi'
    male|a||Where a real comparison sits depends on who chose coverage, and why.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:c431co'
    'male|a||Medicaid is taken up mostly by people who are sick, or expect to be, so the insured would have been less healthy anyway: the bias is negative.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ls5rwp'
    male|a||Among better-off families, coverage of any kind often sorts people the other way.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1la5z1y'
    male|a||For instance, in a 2009 national survey of married couples, those with any insurance rated their health higher than the uninsured did.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1wtqc75'
    male|a||They also had about three more years of schooling, and more than twice the income.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1kspxlx'
    male|a||People like that would have been healthier without coverage too, so there the bias is positive, and the raw gap flatters insurance.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:sj7uls'
    male|a||A new case. Older people who get a flu shot die less often over the winter than those who don't. Which way does selection push that comparison?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:saxtts'
    'male|a||In its favour: the frail and housebound skip the shot more often, so the vaccinated would have died less anyway.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||There is even a tell. In a Washington State study of seventy thousand seniors, the vaccinated were less than half as likely to die before the flu season had begun.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10120
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||A vaccine cannot protect against a flu that has not arrived, so that whole gap is who chose the shot.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1u67kxq'
    'male|a||The usual cure for selection bias is to compare only people who are alike: the same age, the same income, the same recorded diagnoses.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11080
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Then the bias is taken inside each group of look-alikes, X for what was recorded, and every difference the data can see drops out.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1x5cuib'
    'male|a||But people sign up for reasons no survey writes down: a cough that won''t go away, a lump, a bad winter.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1l0edkx'
    male|a||Inside every group of look-alikes, those reasons still steer the sicker into coverage, so the bias shrinks but rarely vanishes.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:19shtyc'
    'male|a||In our town the bias was minus seven. Say the controls swap the uninsured for look-alikes who report only eighteen good days: the bias shrinks to minus three.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:choa6s'
    'male|a||Then the controlled comparison reads eighteen minus eighteen: zero, and coverage looks useless.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:17ee2ia'
    male|a||A quick check. A researcher adds controls, and the insured-minus-uninsured gap moves from minus four to zero. What has she learned?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:11xmixd'
    'male|a||Only that: the shift shows how much the recorded differences mattered, not how much the unrecorded ones still do.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8440
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||So we need to check the controls against an estimate we can trust, and Oregon's study team made that comparison.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7000
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    male|a||Each row is a gap in good days of physical health a month, insured minus uninsured; the dashed line is no difference.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1t8o1q'
    male|a||In national surveys of poor American adults, the insured had about two point three fewer good days.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:6x6y56'
    male|a||Controlling for age, sex, race, education, employment and income cut that to about one fewer.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:d4vf6k'
    male|a||But in Oregon, for the people the lottery moved onto coverage, it added about one and a third good days, give or take about one.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:rtvbx4'
    'male|a||The rows do not describe the same people: Oregon''s lottery entrants about a year on, against poor adults across the country, so the match is rough.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:rgjnx9'
    male|a||If the national effect is near Oregon's, the controls moved the estimate only about a third of the way, and left it on the wrong side of zero.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1oqmb4o'
    male|a||So why can insured people look sicker? Because among the poor, the people who choose coverage would have been sicker without it, and that term outweighs what coverage does.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:pr2g7a'
    'male|a||A raw gap is two terms: what the treatment does, plus how the people who chose it differ.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:5copxt'
    male|a||Who chooses decides which way the second term pushes, and it can be big enough to flip the answer.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1tsajkb'
    male|a||And controls remove only the differences someone recorded, which is why a lottery, blind to everything about people, is worth so much.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:lp5y0g'
    'male|a||Every method in causal inference is a way of borrowing that one number nobody sees: how the treated would have done without it.':
